IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT `cpp-core`
IMPORT `cpp-core-calendar`
IMPORT `cr2-nouns`

-- Canada Pension Plan Regulations (C.R.C., c. 385), Part V -- DISABILITY (regulations 68 to 73).
-- Layer 1: the law, objectively. Source: the Regulations text file, lines 665 to 722.
--
-- What an applicant supplies about a claimed disability and what the Minister may require of the person (68, 69);
-- "substantially gainful" (68.1); failing without good cause to comply (70); telling the Minister of a return to
-- work (70.1); asking for reinstatement of a disability pension and what goes with the request (71, 72). Regulation 73 is repealed.
-- A duty the text puts on a person is a BOOLEAN saying the duty arises; a power of the Minister is a BOOLEAN saying the
-- power exists; a judgment the text hands to the Minister ("deems necessary", "is of the opinion") is a BOOLEAN input.

§ `Part V -- Disability (regulations 68 to 72)`

§§ `Regulation 68(1) -- what the applicant supplies`

-- src:666 | 68 (1) Where an applicant claims that he or some other person is disabled within the meaning of the Act, he shall supply the Minister with the following information in respect of the person whose disability is to be determined:
-- src:667 | (a) a report of any physical or mental disability including
-- src:668 | (i) the nature, extent and prognosis of the disability,
-- src:669 | (ii) the findings upon which the diagnosis and prognosis were made,
-- src:670 | (iii) any limitation resulting from the disability, and
-- src:671 | (iv) any other pertinent information, including recommendations for further diagnostic work or treatment, that may be relevant;
-- src:672 | (b) a statement of that person’s occupation and earnings for the period commencing on the date upon which the applicant alleges that the disability commenced; and
-- src:673 | (c) a statement of that person’s education, employment experience and activities of daily life.
@ref Reg 68(1) (src:666-673)
GIVETH A LIST OF `cr2 Item of information on a claimed disability under regulation 68(1)`
`reg 68(1) — the items the applicant has to supply` MEANS
    LIST `reg 68(1)(a)(i) — a report of the nature, extent and prognosis of the disability`
       , `reg 68(1)(a)(ii) — a report of the findings upon which the diagnosis and prognosis were made`
       , `reg 68(1)(a)(iii) — a report of any limitation resulting from the disability`
       , `reg 68(1)(a)(iv) — a report of any other pertinent information, including recommendations for further diagnostic work or treatment`
       , `reg 68(1)(b) — a statement of the person's occupation and earnings for the period commencing on the date the applicant alleges the disability commenced`
       , `reg 68(1)(c) — a statement of the person's education, employment experience and activities of daily life`

@ref Reg 68(1) (src:666-673)
GIVEN `the applicant claims that the applicant or some other person is disabled within the meaning of the Act` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the items already supplied` IS A LIST OF `cr2 Item of information on a claimed disability under regulation 68(1)`
GIVETH A LIST OF `cr2 Item of information on a claimed disability under regulation 68(1)`
`reg 68(1) — the items the applicant still has to supply`
    `the applicant claims that the applicant or some other person is disabled within the meaning of the Act`
    `the items already supplied` MEANS
    IF `the applicant claims that the applicant or some other person is disabled within the meaning of the Act`
    THEN filter (GIVEN item YIELD NOT (elem item `the items already supplied`)) `reg 68(1) — the items the applicant has to supply`
    ELSE EMPTY

§§ `Regulation 68(2) to (4) -- what the Minister may require, and who bears the cost`

-- src:674 | (2) In addition to the requirements of subsection (1), a person whose disability is to be or has been determined pursuant to the Act may be required from time to time by the Minister
-- src:675 | (a) to supply a statement of his occupation and earnings for any period; and
-- src:676 | (b) to undergo such special examinations and to supply such reports as the Minister deems necessary for the purpose of determining the disability of that person.
@ref Reg 68(2)(a) (src:675)
GIVEN `the person's disability is to be or has been determined pursuant to the Act` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`reg 68(2)(a) — the Minister may require the person to supply a statement of occupation and earnings for any period`
    `the person's disability is to be or has been determined pursuant to the Act` MEANS
    `the person's disability is to be or has been determined pursuant to the Act`

@ref Reg 68(2)(b) (src:676)
GIVEN `the person's disability is to be or has been determined pursuant to the Act` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the Minister deems the examination or report necessary for the purpose of determining the disability` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`reg 68(2)(b) — the Minister may require the person to undergo special examinations and to supply reports`
    `the person's disability is to be or has been determined pursuant to the Act`
    `the Minister deems the examination or report necessary for the purpose of determining the disability` MEANS
    `the person's disability is to be or has been determined pursuant to the Act`
        AND `the Minister deems the examination or report necessary for the purpose of determining the disability`

-- src:677 | (3) The reasonable cost of any examination or report required under subsection (2) shall be
-- src:678 | (a) paid by way of reimbursement or advance, as the Minister deems fit;
-- src:679 | (b) paid out of the Consolidated Revenue Fund; and
-- src:680 | (c) charged to the Canada Pension Plan Account as a cost of administration of the Act.
@ref Reg 68(3) (src:677-680)
GIVEN `the examination or report is required under subsection (2)` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the cost is reasonable` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`reg 68(3)(a) — the reasonable cost is paid by way of reimbursement or advance, as the Minister deems fit`
    `the examination or report is required under subsection (2)` `the cost is reasonable` MEANS
    `the examination or report is required under subsection (2)` AND `the cost is reasonable`

@ref Reg 68(3)(b) (src:679)
GIVEN `the examination or report is required under subsection (2)` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the cost is reasonable` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`reg 68(3)(b) — the reasonable cost is paid out of the Consolidated Revenue Fund`
    `the examination or report is required under subsection (2)` `the cost is reasonable` MEANS
    `the examination or report is required under subsection (2)` AND `the cost is reasonable`

@ref Reg 68(3)(c) (src:680)
GIVEN `the examination or report is required under subsection (2)` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the cost is reasonable` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`reg 68(3)(c) — the reasonable cost is charged to the Canada Pension Plan Account as a cost of administration of the Act`
    `the examination or report is required under subsection (2)` `the cost is reasonable` MEANS
    `the examination or report is required under subsection (2)` AND `the cost is reasonable`

-- src:681 | (4) For the purposes of this section, cost includes travel and living expenses that the Minister deems necessary of the person whose disability is to be determined and of a person to accompany that person.
@ref Reg 68(4) (src:681)
GIVEN `the expense is a travel or living expense of the person whose disability is to be determined or of a person to accompany that person` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the Minister deems the expense necessary` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`reg 68(4) — the expense is included in the cost`
    `the expense is a travel or living expense of the person whose disability is to be determined or of a person to accompany that person`
    `the Minister deems the expense necessary` MEANS
    `the expense is a travel or living expense of the person whose disability is to be determined or of a person to accompany that person`
        AND `the Minister deems the expense necessary`

§§ `Regulation 68.1 -- substantially gainful`

-- 68.1(2): a fraction of a cent is rounded to the nearest whole cent, and to the higher of two where equidistant.
-- src:682 | 68.1 (1) For the purpose of subparagraph 42(2)(a)(i) of the Act, substantially gainful, in respect of an occupation, describes an occupation that provides a salary or wages equal to or greater than the maximum annual amount a person could receive as a disability pension. The amount is determined by the formula
-- src:683 | (A × B) + C
-- src:684 | where
-- src:685 | A is .25 × the Maximum Pensionable Earnings Average;
-- src:686 | B is .75; and
-- src:687 | C is the flat rate benefit, calculated as provided in subsection 56(2) of the Act, × 12.
-- src:688 | (2) If the amount calculated under subsection (1) contains a fraction of a cent, the amount is to be rounded to the nearest whole cent or, if the amount is equidistant from two whole cents, to the higher of them.
@ref Reg 68.1(2) (src:688)
GIVEN amount IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`reg 68.1(2) — an amount rounded to the nearest whole cent` amount MEANS
    FLOOR ((amount TIMES 100) PLUS 0.5) DIVIDED BY 100

-- 68.1(1): (A x B) + C, where A is .25 x the Maximum Pensionable Earnings Average, B is .75 and C is the flat rate benefit x 12.
@ref Reg 68.1(1) (src:682-687)
GIVEN `the Maximum Pensionable Earnings Average` IS A NUMBER   -- out of range: section 42(1) (piece cp3)
      `the flat rate benefit calculated as provided in subsection 56(2) of the Act` IS A NUMBER   -- out of range: section 56(2) (piece cp4)
GIVETH A NUMBER
`reg 68.1(1) — the maximum annual amount a person could receive as a disability pension`
    `the Maximum Pensionable Earnings Average`
    `the flat rate benefit calculated as provided in subsection 56(2) of the Act` MEANS
    `reg 68.1(2) — an amount rounded to the nearest whole cent`
        (((0.25 TIMES `the Maximum Pensionable Earnings Average`) TIMES 0.75)
         PLUS (`the flat rate benefit calculated as provided in subsection 56(2) of the Act` TIMES 12))

@ref Reg 68.1(1) (src:682-687)
GIVEN `the salary or wages the occupation provides in a year` IS A NUMBER
      `the Maximum Pensionable Earnings Average` IS A NUMBER
      `the flat rate benefit calculated as provided in subsection 56(2) of the Act` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`reg 68.1(1) — an occupation is substantially gainful`
    `the salary or wages the occupation provides in a year`
    `the Maximum Pensionable Earnings Average`
    `the flat rate benefit calculated as provided in subsection 56(2) of the Act` MEANS
    `the salary or wages the occupation provides in a year` AT LEAST
        (`reg 68.1(1) — the maximum annual amount a person could receive as a disability pension`
            `the Maximum Pensionable Earnings Average` `the flat rate benefit calculated as provided in subsection 56(2) of the Act`)

§§ `Regulation 69 -- the person determined to be disabled`

-- src:689 | 69 (1) For the purpose of determining whether any amount shall be paid or shall continue to be paid as a benefit in respect of a person who has been determined to be disabled within the meaning of the Act, the Minister may require that person from time to time
-- src:690 | (a) to undergo such special examinations,
-- src:691 | (b) to supply such reports, and
-- src:692 | (c) to supply such statements of his occupation and earnings for any period,
-- src:693 | as the Minister may specify.
@ref Reg 69(1) (src:689-693)
GIVEN `the person has been determined to be disabled within the meaning of the Act` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the Minister requires it for the purpose of determining whether any amount shall be paid or shall continue to be paid as a benefit` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`reg 69(1) — the Minister may require the person to undergo special examinations, supply reports and supply statements of occupation and earnings`
    `the person has been determined to be disabled within the meaning of the Act`
    `the Minister requires it for the purpose of determining whether any amount shall be paid or shall continue to be paid as a benefit` MEANS
    `the person has been determined to be disabled within the meaning of the Act`
        AND `the Minister requires it for the purpose of determining whether any amount shall be paid or shall continue to be paid as a benefit`

-- src:694 | (2) Where the Minister is of the opinion that a person who has been determined to be disabled within the meaning of the Act may benefit vocationally from reasonable rehabilitation measures, he may, from time to time, require that person to undergo such reasonable rehabilitation measures as he may specify.
@ref Reg 69(2) (src:694)
GIVEN `the person has been determined to be disabled within the meaning of the Act` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the Minister is of the opinion that the person may benefit vocationally from reasonable rehabilitation measures` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`reg 69(2) — the Minister may require the person to undergo reasonable rehabilitation measures`
    `the person has been determined to be disabled within the meaning of the Act`
    `the Minister is of the opinion that the person may benefit vocationally from reasonable rehabilitation measures` MEANS
    `the person has been determined to be disabled within the meaning of the Act`
        AND `the Minister is of the opinion that the person may benefit vocationally from reasonable rehabilitation measures`

-- src:695 | (3) The reasonable cost of any examination or report or rehabilitation measure required under this section shall be
-- src:696 | (a) paid by way of reimbursement or advance, as the Minister deems fit;
-- src:697 | (b) paid out of the Consolidated Revenue Fund; and
-- src:698 | (c) charged to the Canada Pension Plan Account as a cost of administration of the Act.
@ref Reg 69(3) (src:695-698)
GIVEN `the examination, report or rehabilitation measure is required under this section` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the cost is reasonable` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`reg 69(3)(a) — the reasonable cost is paid by way of reimbursement or advance, as the Minister deems fit`
    `the examination, report or rehabilitation measure is required under this section` `the cost is reasonable` MEANS
    `the examination, report or rehabilitation measure is required under this section` AND `the cost is reasonable`

@ref Reg 69(3)(b) (src:697)
GIVEN `the examination, report or rehabilitation measure is required under this section` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the cost is reasonable` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`reg 69(3)(b) — the reasonable cost is paid out of the Consolidated Revenue Fund`
    `the examination, report or rehabilitation measure is required under this section` `the cost is reasonable` MEANS
    `the examination, report or rehabilitation measure is required under this section` AND `the cost is reasonable`

@ref Reg 69(3)(c) (src:698)
GIVEN `the examination, report or rehabilitation measure is required under this section` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the cost is reasonable` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`reg 69(3)(c) — the reasonable cost is charged to the Canada Pension Plan Account as a cost of administration of the Act`
    `the examination, report or rehabilitation measure is required under this section` `the cost is reasonable` MEANS
    `the examination, report or rehabilitation measure is required under this section` AND `the cost is reasonable`

-- src:699 | (4) For the purposes of this section, cost includes travel and living expenses that the Minister deems necessary of the disabled person and of a person to accompany that person.
@ref Reg 69(4) (src:699)
GIVEN `the expense is a travel or living expense of the disabled person or of a person to accompany that person` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the Minister deems the expense necessary` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`reg 69(4) — the expense is included in the cost`
    `the expense is a travel or living expense of the disabled person or of a person to accompany that person`
    `the Minister deems the expense necessary` MEANS
    `the expense is a travel or living expense of the disabled person or of a person to accompany that person`
        AND `the Minister deems the expense necessary`

§§ `Regulation 70 -- failing to comply without good cause`

-- src:700 | 70 (1) Where a person who has been determined to be disabled within the meaning of the Act fails without good cause to comply with any requirement of the Minister made under section 69, he may be determined to have ceased to be disabled at such time as the Minister may specify except that such time shall not be earlier than the day of failure to comply.
-- src:701 | (2) For the purpose of subsection (1), good cause means a significant risk to a person’s life or health.
@ref Reg 70(2) (src:701)
GIVEN `compliance would present a significant risk to the person's life or health` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`reg 70(2) — the failure to comply is for good cause` `compliance would present a significant risk to the person's life or health` MEANS
    `compliance would present a significant risk to the person's life or health`

@ref Reg 70(1) (src:700)
GIVEN `the person has been determined to be disabled within the meaning of the Act` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person failed to comply with a requirement of the Minister made under section 69` IS A BOOLEAN
      `compliance would present a significant risk to the person's life or health` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`reg 70(1) — the person may be determined to have ceased to be disabled`
    `the person has been determined to be disabled within the meaning of the Act`
    `the person failed to comply with a requirement of the Minister made under section 69`
    `compliance would present a significant risk to the person's life or health` MEANS
    `the person has been determined to be disabled within the meaning of the Act`
        AND `the person failed to comply with a requirement of the Minister made under section 69`
        AND (NOT (`reg 70(2) — the failure to comply is for good cause` `compliance would present a significant risk to the person's life or health`))

@ref Reg 70(1) (src:700)
GIVEN `the day of the failure to comply` IS A DATE
      `the time the Minister specifies` IS A DATE
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`reg 70(1) — the time the Minister specifies is not earlier than the day of failure to comply`
    `the day of the failure to comply` `the time the Minister specifies` MEANS
    `the time the Minister specifies` AT LEAST `the day of the failure to comply`

§§ `Regulation 70.1 -- return to work`

-- src:704 | 70.1 If a person who has been determined to be disabled within the meaning of the Act returns to work, the person shall so inform the Minister without delay.
@ref Reg 70.1 (src:704)
GIVEN `the person has been determined to be disabled within the meaning of the Act` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person returns to work` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`reg 70.1 — the person must inform the Minister without delay`
    `the person has been determined to be disabled within the meaning of the Act` `the person returns to work` MEANS
    `the person has been determined to be disabled within the meaning of the Act` AND `the person returns to work`

§§ `Regulations 71 and 72 -- request for reinstatement of a disability pension`

-- src:707 | 71 (1) A request for reinstatement of a disability pension or a post-retirement disability benefit under section 70.1 of the Act shall be made by submitting it to the Minister in writing.
-- src:708 | (2) The request shall be made within 12 months after the month in which the person became incapable again of working.
@ref Reg 71(1) (src:707)
GIVEN `the request is submitted to the Minister in writing` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`reg 71(1) — a request for reinstatement is made as the Regulations require` `the request is submitted to the Minister in writing` MEANS
    `the request is submitted to the Minister in writing`

-- 71(2): within 12 months after the month in which the person became incapable again of working: the last day is the last day
-- of the 12th month after that month (fork F-46.2 applies to the counting).
@ref Reg 71(2) (src:708)
GIVEN `a day in the month in which the person became incapable again of working` IS A DATE
GIVETH A DATE
`reg 71(2) — the last day to make the request` `a day in the month in which the person became incapable again of working` MEANS
    `the month following the month of a date` (`add months` (`the month of a date` `a day in the month in which the person became incapable again of working`) 12) PLUS (0 MINUS 1)

@ref Reg 71(2) (src:708)
GIVEN `a day in the month in which the person became incapable again of working` IS A DATE
      `the date of the request` IS A DATE
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`reg 71(2) — the request is made in time` `a day in the month in which the person became incapable again of working` `the date of the request` MEANS
    `the date of the request` AT LEAST (`the month of a date` `a day in the month in which the person became incapable again of working`)
        AND `the date of the request` AT MOST
            (`reg 71(2) — the last day to make the request` `a day in the month in which the person became incapable again of working`)

-- src:709 | 72 (1) The determination as to whether a person is entitled to have a disability pension or a post-retirement disability benefit reinstated shall be made by the Minister on the basis of the information and the evidence provided to the Minister under subsection (2).
@ref Reg 72(1) (src:709)
GIVEN `the determination is whether a person is entitled to have a disability pension or a post-retirement disability benefit reinstated` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`reg 72(1) — the Minister must decide on the information and evidence furnished under subsection (2)`
    `the determination is whether a person is entitled to have a disability pension or a post-retirement disability benefit reinstated` MEANS
    `the determination is whether a person is entitled to have a disability pension or a post-retirement disability benefit reinstated`

-- 72(2) (a) to (f) are always required; (g) only if the request includes a request to reinstate the disabled contributor's child
-- benefit in respect of each of the applicant's children who are 18 years of age or more. The text states this condition itself,
-- so the list that applies is worked out (unlike regulations 46, 52 to 54.1).
-- src:710 | (2) The applicant or the person making a request on the applicant’s behalf shall furnish the Minister with the following information and evidence:
-- src:711 | (a) the applicant’s name, address and Social Insurance Number and, if applicable, the name and address of the person making the request on the applicant’s behalf and that person’s relationship to the applicant;
-- src:712 | (b) the month in which the applicant ceased to receive the disability pension or post-retirement disability benefit;
-- src:713 | (c) the month in which the applicant became incapable again of working;
-- src:714 | (d) the date that the applicant stopped working;
-- src:715 | (e) the statement of a person qualified to practise medicine confirming that the applicant has a severe and prolonged mental or physical disability that is the same as, or is related to, the disability that entitled the applicant to receive the disability pension or post-retirement disability benefit that is the subject of the request;
-- src:716 | (f) the name of each dependent child of the applicant and whether they are a child in respect of whom, either legally or in fact, the applicant has at least 20% of the parenting time; and
-- src:717 | (g) if the request includes a request to reinstate the disabled contributor’s child benefit in respect of each of the applicant’s children who are 18 years of age or more,
-- src:718 | (i) the child’s name, address and Social Insurance Number, and
-- src:719 | (ii) evidence, established in accordance with section 67, that the child is in full-time or part-time attendance at a school or university.
@ref Reg 72(2) (src:710-719)
GIVEN `the request includes a request to reinstate the disabled contributor's child benefit for children aged 18 or more` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A LIST OF `cr2 Item of information on a request for reinstatement under regulation 72(2)`
`reg 72(2) — the items the applicant has to furnish` `the request includes a request to reinstate the disabled contributor's child benefit for children aged 18 or more` MEANS
    append
        (LIST `reg 72(2)(a) — the applicant's name, address and Social Insurance Number and, if applicable, the name and address of the person making the request for the applicant and that person's relationship to the applicant`
            , `reg 72(2)(b) — the month in which the applicant ceased to receive the disability pension or post-retirement disability benefit`
            , `reg 72(2)(c) — the month in which the applicant became incapable again of working`
            , `reg 72(2)(d) — the date that the applicant stopped working`
            , `reg 72(2)(e) — the statement of a person qualified to practise medicine confirming a severe and prolonged disability that is the same as, or related to, the disability that entitled the applicant to the pension or benefit`
            , `reg 72(2)(f) — the name of each dependent child of the applicant and whether the applicant has at least 20% of the parenting time in respect of the child`)
        (IF `the request includes a request to reinstate the disabled contributor's child benefit for children aged 18 or more`
         THEN LIST `reg 72(2)(g)(i) — for each child aged 18 or more whose disabled contributor's child benefit is to be reinstated, the child's name, address and Social Insurance Number`
                 , `reg 72(2)(g)(ii) — for each such child, evidence, established in accordance with section 67, of full-time or part-time attendance at a school or university`
         ELSE EMPTY)

@ref Reg 72(2) (src:710-719)
GIVEN `the request includes a request to reinstate the disabled contributor's child benefit for children aged 18 or more` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the items already furnished` IS A LIST OF `cr2 Item of information on a request for reinstatement under regulation 72(2)`
GIVETH A LIST OF `cr2 Item of information on a request for reinstatement under regulation 72(2)`
`reg 72(2) — the items the applicant still has to furnish`
    `the request includes a request to reinstate the disabled contributor's child benefit for children aged 18 or more`
    `the items already furnished` MEANS
    filter (GIVEN item YIELD NOT (elem item `the items already furnished`))
        (`reg 72(2) — the items the applicant has to furnish` `the request includes a request to reinstate the disabled contributor's child benefit for children aged 18 or more`)
